    "body": "The patch-only archive was not reliably restorable: a test on 2026-10-09 applied 0 of 6 as plain patches and 1 of 6 with a three-way apply, because the branches were cut from older merge bases, main has moved since, and some content is already on main. RECORDING work is not the same as being able to RESTORE it, so this adds the reliable form. deepseek-branches.bundle is VERIFIED: 'git bundle verify' reports a complete history, and fetching it into a scratch clone restored all six branches with tips matching the originals (entry-isolation 1d98faaea, d20-run d5172e7f6, and four more). It is ~115 MB because it carries the complete object closure of the six branches, which is exactly what makes it independent of this repository's history; GitHub rejects any single file above 100 MB, so it is stored as ds-bundle.part00 (90 MB) and ds-bundle.part01 (25 MB) with the reassembly command, the failed approaches and the size documented in INDEX.txt. The branch is rebuilt from efcfe3cd0, so the oversized single-file blob never enters branch history. References #820",
